--- PAGE 1 of 5: HOW TO PLAY, PHASES 1 & 2 ---

MESOS - HOW TO PLAY
A game of MESOS unfolds over 10 rounds until the Tribe cards deck is depleted. In each round, carry out the following two phases in order.

PHASE 1: PLACE TOTEM PAWNS
Following the order of the Totem pawns on the Turn Order tile from top to bottom, place your Totem on an available Offer tile (i.e., a tile where there is no other Totem already).

Each Offer tile shows:
- A space where you can place your Totem
- The action you must perform (usually the number of cards you can take and the row from where you can take them)
- A letter indicating the tile's position on the Offer track

PHASE 2: RESOLVE ACTIONS
In turn, starting from the player with the leftmost Totem on the Offer track and proceeding right, resolve the action indicated on your Offer tile. With the exception of tile A (5-player games only, provides 3 Food), all other Offer tiles let you choose and take Character 🧍 and/or Building cards 🏠 from the upper and/or lower row as indicated. You can never take Event cards. If multiple cards are allowed, choose the order freely. If no cards are available in the required rows, you receive nothing. If cards are available, you must take them. After resolving your action, return your Totem to the Turn Order tile, placing it in the first available space from the top. If that space provides a Food bonus, take the specified Food tokens immediately. The player in the last space must pay 1 Food (or lose 2 PP 🌟 if they have none). The Totem arrangement on the Turn Order tile sets the turn order for the next round.

FOOD🍖 AND PRESTIGE POINTS🌟
Whenever you take Food, place the corresponding Food tokens in your personal supply. When paying Food, return them to the general supply. Whenever you gain Prestige Points (PP 🌟), take tokens from the general supply. When you lose PP 🌟, return them. If your score goes negative, use the reverse side of the PP 🌟 tokens.

--- PAGE 2 of 5: CHARACTER CARDS 🧍 & BUILDING CARDS 🏠 ---

TAKING CHARACTER CARDS 🧍
When you take a Character card 🧍, add it to your tribe by placing it in front of you in columns of the same color, leaving only the icons in the top corners visible. Adding Character cards 🧍 has no cost; however, during Sustenance you must have enough Food to feed them all or lose PP 🌟.

There are 6 types of Character cards 🧍:

INVENTORS [INV]
At the end of the game, Inventors provide a number of PP 🌟 equal to the number of Inventors in your tribe multiplied by the number of different Invention icons you have. There are 10 different Invention icons.

GATHERERS [GAT]
During the Sustenance Event, they provide a discount of 3 Food on the total you would have to pay. Note: You do not take any Food from Gatherers under any circumstances.

SHAMANS [SHA]
Shamans can show from 1 to 3 icons. During the Shamanic Ritual Event, having the majority of these icons provides PP 🌟; having the minority results in losing PP 🌟.

BUILDERS [BLD]
During the game, each Builder reduces the Food cost of every Building card 🏠 you take by the amount indicated in the top right corner. At the end of the game, each Builder provides the PP 🌟 indicated in the lower left corner.

ARTISTS [ART]
During the Cave Paintings Event, you can gain or lose PP 🌟 based on the number of Artists in your tribe. At the end of the game, you gain 10 PP 🌟 for every 2 (or 3+) Artists in your tribe.

--- PAGE 3 of 5: END OF ROUND & EVENTS ---

TAKING BUILDING CARDS 🏠
When you take a Building card 🏠, you must pay the Food cost indicated in the top left corner and then add it to your tribe. If you don't have the required Food, you cannot take it. Each Builder reduces the cost; sum all discounts, but you can never reduce below zero.
Each Building card 🏠 shows: Food cost, PP 🌟 at end of game, and a special effect.

END OF THE ROUND
After all players have finished their turns, perform the following steps in order:

STEP 1 - RESOLVE EVENTS
If there are Event cards in the bottom row, resolve them. If Sustenance is among them, resolve it last. In the rare case of two Events of the same type in one round, resolve them in Era order. There are 4 Event cards (Hunt, Shamanic Ritual, Cave Paintings, Sustenance) in each Era, with increasing values from one Era to the next. You cannot take Event cards to add to your tribe.

SUSTENANCE [SUS]
Pay 1 Food token for each Character card 🧍 in your tribe (Building cards 🏠 do not count). If you cannot feed all your Characters 🧍, lose the PP 🌟 indicated on the Event card for each Character 🧍 you couldn't feed. You cannot choose to lose PP 🌟 to avoid paying Food. Keep all your Characters 🧍 regardless. Each Gatherer gives a discount of 3 Food. Sustenance must always be resolved last.

HUNT [HNT]
Take 1 Food token and gain the PP 🌟 indicated on the Event card for each Hunter in your tribe.

SHAMANIC RITUAL [RIT]
The player with the most icons gains the PP 🌟 indicated on the Event card. The player with fewest icons loses the indicated PP 🌟. In case of a tie, all tied players gain or lose the indicated PP 🌟.

CAVE PAINTINGS [PAI]
To gain PP 🌟 you must have a minimum number of Artists as indicated by the Event card. If you have fewer Artists than the number shown in the top line, you lose the indicated PP 🌟. If you have the number shown in the lower line or more, you gain the indicated PP 🌟 for each of your Artists.

--- PAGE 4 of 5: BEGINNING OF NEW ERA & END GAME ---

END-OF-ROUND STEPS (CONTINUED)
Step 2: Discard all Character 🧍 and Event cards in the bottom row. Building cards 🏠 in the bottom row remain in place.
Step 3: Move all remaining Character 🧍 and Event cards from the top row to the bottom row. Building cards 🏠 remain in place.
Step 4: Restore the top row. Draw from the Tribe deck a number of cards equal to the number of players plus 4 and place them above the Offer track to create a new top row.

BEGINNING OF A NEW ERA
As soon as you reveal a Tribe card from the next Era while restoring the top row, the new Era begins and:
Step 1: Discard any Building cards 🏠 in the bottom row. This happens only at the beginning of Era III.
Step 2: Move any Building cards 🏠 from the top row to the bottom row, placing them to the right of Tribe cards. This happens at the beginning of Era II and III.
Step 3: Place Building cards 🏠 from the just-started Era in the top row to the right of Tribe cards, face up. This happens at the beginning of Era II and III.
Afterward, proceed as usual with a new round.

END GAME
The game ends at the end of the 10th round when the Tribe deck is depleted. At the end of this final round, resolve all visible Events including those in the top row. Sustenance must be resolved last.

FINAL SCORING - ADD THE FOLLOWING PP 🌟:
- PP 🌟 from Builders in your tribe
- 10 PP 🌟 for every 2 Artists in your tribe
- PP 🌟 equal to Inventors x number of different Invention icons on their cards
- PP 🌟 from Buildings in your tribe (card PP 🌟 + endgame effects)

The player with the most PP 🌟 wins. Tiebreak: most Food. Further tie: shared victory.

--- PAGE 5 of 5: BUILDING CARDS APPENDIX ---

BUILDING CARDS - APPENDIX

1. [+5🍖x🌈] Every time you complete a set of 6 different Character cards 🧍, take 5 Food tokens. (Does not apply to sets already completed before acquiring the Building 🏠.)

2. [SUS: -1🍖x🧍] During Sustenance, discount of 1 Food per Artist, Inventor, or Gatherer in your tribe.

3. [RIT:🛡️] During Shamanic Ritual, you do not lose PP 🌟 even if you have fewer STAR icons than all other players.

4. [🗿+🍖] When you move your Totem to a space with a Food bonus, take 1 additional Food token. (No effect for the last space)

5. [+3🍖x2INV] Every time you obtain a pair of identical Inventors (same icon), take 3 Food tokens. (Does not apply to pairs already owned before acquiring this Building 🏠.)

6. [RIT: +3★] During Shamanic Ritual, your tribe has 3 additional STAR icons.

7. [RIT: x2🌟] During Shamanic Ritual, if you have more STAR icons than any other player, you gain double the PP 🌟. You still gain PP 🌟 in case of a tie.

8. [HNT: +1🍖+1🌟xHUN] During Hunt, take 1 Food and gain 1 additional PP 🌟 for each Hunter in your tribe.

9. [🏁 2xBLD🌟] At the end of the game, you gain double the PP 🌟 from Builder cards 🏠 in your tribe.

10. [PAI: +1🍖xART] During Cave Paintings, take 1 Food for each Artist in your tribe.

11. [🏁 6🌟x🌈] At the end of the game, gain 6 PP 🌟 for each complete set of 6 different Character cards 🧍 in your tribe.

12. [🏁 +N🍖x🧍] At the end of the game, gain the indicated PP 🌟 for each indicated Character card 🧍 in your tribe.

13. [+1 ⏩] After all Totems are moved back to the Turn Order tile (before the End of Round phase), you may take 1 Character 🧍 or 1 Building card 🏠 (paying its cost) from the top row.

14. [🏁 +25🌟] At the end of the game, you gain 25 Prestige Points (PP 🌟).